@@ -1286,6 +1286,32 @@
    - `"wait"`: omit that cooperative steering signal and let side-effecting work finish before injecting steering at the tool-batch boundary
    - In both modes, interruptible waits are cancelled or skipped when steering arrives. This setting is not equivalent to `abort`.
 
+## Native editor completion
+
+A runtime advertising `ready.capabilities.commandCompletion.version = 1` accepts
+`complete` with `{text, cursor}`. `text` is the full editor input, and `cursor` is
+an offset in UTF-16 code units. Lookup never submits a prompt or runs a command.
+
+The response data is `{supported: true, items}`. Each item contains a request-local
+`id`, `label`, `insertText`, `replaceRange: {start, end}`, the resulting `cursor`,
+and `triggerCompletion`; descriptions, hints and kinds are optional. Apply the
+exact edit only while the input and caret still match the request, then query
+again when `triggerCompletion` is true. An empty list is authoritative. Edits
+that leave both text and caret unchanged are omitted so Enter can submit a
+completed command.
+
+The same session-owned native completer is available over ACP when initialize
+advertises `_meta.ompCommandCompletion.version = 1`, through
+`_omp/commands/complete` with `{sessionId, text, cursor}`. Builtin handlers,
+extension callbacks and provider factories share the original completion code.
+TUI-only commands and completions requiring local `onApplied` callbacks are
+excluded; remote lookup must not perform these UI side effects.
+
+Inputs and resulting editor text are limited to 64 KiB, candidates to 256 and
+serialized candidate data to 896 KiB. Lookup has a 750 ms budget; a newer lookup
+cancels the preceding one. Invalid UTF-16 boundaries and lookup failures return
+errors rather than falling back to fabricated suggestions.
+
 ## Extension UI Sub-Protocol
 
 Extensions in RPC mode use request/response UI frames. `--no-ui` disables the extension runner's UI in both RPC modes: extensions see `ctx.hasUI === false`, dialogs resolve to their defaults without emitting frames, and presentation updates (`notify`, `setStatus`, `setWidget`, `setTitle`, `set_editor_text`) are dropped.
